1
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,960
Oh

2
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,270
Dumpfrog!

3
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:05,600
Don't burrow me, you big slimy jerk!

4
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:09,508
You realize that slap of yours
derailed our train, don't you?

5
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,740
Froggy, turn back!

6
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,098
Get out of the way!

7
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:18,020
We were about to catch up with Sanji, too!

8
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,540
Now apologize!

9
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:25,450
Dumpfrog!

10
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,960
I'm gonna beat you!

11
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:37,217
I don't know what's going on out
there right now, but it can't be good.

12
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,947
Hey, are you guys all right?

13
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,000
I guess so.

14
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:45,410
Help!

15
00:02:45,493 --> 00:02:46,500
My back!

16
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,320
Oh, no!

17
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:52,660
Our King Bulls are gone!

18
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,120
They disappeared!

19
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:57,940
No way! But how?

20
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,620
No, we're the ones who disappeared.

21
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:03,900
Our train probably got
derailed back there. Ah!

22
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:07,660
Whoa, that's even worse! What now? Hey!

23
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,070
Yeah?

24
00:03:09,153 --> 00:03:11,040
Are we gonna be okay or what?

25
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:15,197
If we can't make it to Annie's lobby,
I'm gonna be really pissed off!

26
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:18,940
Shut your trap and give me
a second, try it to work!

27
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,820
Oh, that's weird.

28
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:24,017
I think there's something funny
going on with this current.

29
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,460
Seems like we're stuck.

30
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:27,220
Kokoro? Huh?

31
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,357
Do you know which direction to go?

32
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,740
Yeah, of course I do.

33
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:34,437
When we built the sea trains, we
equipped them with eternal poses?

34
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,167
set to all the islands
with stations on them.

35
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,480
Then we'll be fine.

36
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:41,540
I'll watch the sea, you just steer. Huh?

37
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,220
You sure that'll help?

38
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,457
I'm a navigator.

39
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:48,677
I got this I see yeah that's

40
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:55,500
good to know oh almost
forgot Hey, Yokozuna!

41
00:03:55,820 --> 00:04:00,380
Stop wrestling and get your froggy
butt off of here! Well... Get her!

42
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:03,940
Get her!

43
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,860
Get away!

44
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:13,860
What was that?

45
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,628
You're glad I'm still okay?

46
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,620
How sweet.

47
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:20,697
I know you were just trying to
save me, but you jumped the gun.

48
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:22,600
These folks didn't kidnap me.

49
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,300
Does this mean Granny can speak frog?

50
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:28,850
Yeah.

51
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,397
What are you guys looking at?

52
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,700
That ugly old lady is
talking to a giant frog.

53
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:40,540
Oh, I get it, Granny was a frog all along.

54
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:43,377
She never quite passed
as a human now, did she?

55
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:46,357
You realize you guys are gonna
get hit for that later, don't you?

56
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,270
No kidding.

57
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:50,860
Hello, Straw Hat, Rocket Man.

58
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,715
And you see them yet?

59
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,060
No, I got nothing.

60
00:04:55,200 --> 00:05:00,082
Damn, that stupid frog, that thing must
have sent them flying a million miles away.

61
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:02,480
Hey, don't start losing hope on me.

62
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:06,957
We set out to save our bro Franky and
we won't stop till we make it happen.

63
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:07,870
That's right!

64
00:05:07,953 --> 00:05:10,577
All we can do now is keep on
heading to Annie's Lobby and have

65
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:14,189
faith that Rocketman is gonna
meet us whenever we get there!

66
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:16,500
Go! Sodom! Gomorrah!

67
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,090
Huh?

68
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,680
Hey, hold on!

69
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:23,997
What's that over there?

70
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:27,657
It looks like there's another train
car floating just ahead of us.

71
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:29,480
It could be full of enemies.

72
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,720
All right, guys, let's
prepare for battle! Yeah!

73
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,190
Ahoy!

74
00:05:37,273 --> 00:05:38,280
Is anyone in there?

75
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:40,420
We're the Franky family.

76
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:42,568
Come out and show yourself.

77
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,180
Hey, I see someone.

78
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:55,237
What he's really alive you're
not just yanking my chain?

79
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,837
No I heard that he still survived!

80
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:05,277
I say that's good stupid ice for brains

81
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,717
really had me worried for a while there!

82
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,777
I thought he was dead for sure.

83
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:13,577
For the record CP9 might
think that they killed him.

84
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:16,500
I'd keep quiet about it if I were you.

85
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:23,000
You act tough, but you got a
heart in there like anyone else.

86
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,500
Anyway, we're in trouble now.

87
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:33,608
The government's got
exactly what they want.

88
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:37,477
The only woman with the know-how
to bring back an ancient weapon,

89
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,940
and the man with the only
known blueprints for one.

90
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,660
Don't that beat all.

91
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:47,077
If the government
actually gets that power,

92
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,631
everything's gonna get turned upside down.

93
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,617
First, they'll end the pirate era.

94
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,517
We won't be able to fight back anymore.

95
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,306
And after they're done
with us, just you wait.

96
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:59,077
They'll turn their guns
on the rest of the world.

97
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:03,557
I'm telling you, those ancient weapons
are gonna lead all of mankind to ruin.

98
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:08,052
My master didn't lay down his life
protecting those blueprints for nothing.

99
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:11,080
Not if I have anything to
say about it, at least.

100
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:17,567
But still, there's no point in
me making it out of here alone.

101
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:21,252
You gotta find some way to get
back to Straw Hat, alright?

102
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:24,037
I can't.

103
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:27,179
If I'm with them, it will
only bring them suffering.

104
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,517
You're not the one that's hurting them.

105
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:36,537
Those government bastards may tell
you that your existence is a crime,

106
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:40,420
but no matter how dangerous
you may be, just being alive,

107
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,300
just being who you are, is never wrong.

108
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:49,040
Remember, when a ship is
built, no matter what type,

109
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:52,140
it's neither good nor evil, Franky.

110
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,340
You got that?

111
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:59,180
Her very existence has
been nothing but a sin.

112
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:04,620
What you do is your choice, but there's
no right or wrong in who you are.

113
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:14,890
Hmph!

114
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,940
My goodness, just look at you.

115
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,700
You're covered in scars.

116
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:21,720
Poor kid.

117
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:24,800
It's been eight years now.

118
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,740
Eight long years since Tom
was taken away from us.

119
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:32,949
I've watched you challenge the
C train every day since then.

120
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,480
Again and again.

121
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:52,017
You were trying to get stronger weren't
you so you will never have to lose

122
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:55,757
the ones you love ever again so you'll

123
00:08:55,840 --> 00:09:01,660
have the power to protect them don't cry

124
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:06,120
now's the time for you to put
that training to the death big boy

125
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:11,960
You remember your old pal Franky, right?

126
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:15,400
He got taken away by the
bad guys, too, like Tom.

127
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:20,440
The good news is we're on our
way to save him as we speak.

128
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,579
So, are you up for a fight or what?

129
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:32,360
Hey, Starhack, I think I
found another friend for you.

130
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,380
Sounds good to me.

131
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,960
Nice job, Monster Granny!

132
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,260
Wait, where is it? Frog Granny?

133
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:43,500
You gotta tell me these things. Oh?

134
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,800
You call me whatever you like.

135
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:51,797
Kokoro, I found us a good current
for running to the southwest.

136
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:52,860
Alright then.

137
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:58,700
Well, we wasted a little time back
there, but we'll get it back in a flash!

138
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,196
You heard her, Frog!

139
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,580
Let's go!

140
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:10,120
Cape has arrived! Look sharp!

141
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:13,637
Congratulations on
completing your mission!

142
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,837
Bring out the criminals!

143
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:15,979
They're in Call 1!

144
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:22,417
How are you handling it
on a little more cat?

145
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,330
Do you love it?

146
00:10:23,413 --> 00:10:26,680
I come from all of the RPs! Whoa!

147
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,156
Everyone stand back!

148
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,250
Careful!

149
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,163
That guy bites!

150
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,321
You punks want some of this, huh?

151
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:33,290
Come on, get him!

152
00:10:33,373 --> 00:10:34,960
Must he be so noisy?

153
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:44,920
I've never seen them up
close. Pretty intimidating.

154
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,100
That guy's Kaido Flam, right?

155
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:49,520
No way.

156
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:52,940
Then the woman must be Nico Robin.

157
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,480
Wow, she's gorgeous.

158
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,100
Open the main gate!

159
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,420
Whoa, what the hell is this crazy place?

160
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:30,940
A waterfall?

161
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,320
What?

162
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:42,520
I can't see the bottom!

163
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,380
You sure are a noisy one.

164
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:54,560
It looks like Luchi and the
others are headed this way.

165
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:03,860
And they've brought me the best
souvenir I could ever possibly wish for.

166
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:07,820
At last,

167
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:09,780
after five long years,

168
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:14,700
the time has finally come for all
eight members of CP9 to be reunited.

169
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:17,580
This should be a time of celebration.

170
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:19,537
But instead, I'll ask...

171
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,208
What's the meaning of this?

172
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:25,337
Your orders were to assassinate
the leaders of the revolution.

173
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:27,137
But according to this article,

174
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:30,417
not only did you kill those
three, but 20 others as well.

175
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:31,330
What happened?

176
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:33,949
If you have an excuse,
I'd like to hear it!

177
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:35,170
Yo-yo!

178
00:12:35,253 --> 00:12:38,380
My most sincere apologies and pardons.

179
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:46,060
Chief, everything is entirely,
unreservedly, completely my fault.

180
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,580
Stop that, Kumadori.

181
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,249
A real man doesn't bow
his head to anybody.

182
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:53,337
I'll explain everything
that happened to the Chief,

183
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,317
so shut up and get a hold of yourself.

184
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,230
Yo-yo!

185
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:57,857
I can't apologize enough.

186
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:03,560
And so, if need be, I'll shoulder
the blame by taking my own life!

187
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,537
Don't be so melodramatic!

188
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,326
It happened like this, Chief.

189
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,077
We followed the plan to the letter.

190
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:12,077
We infiltrated their forces and were
all ready for the assassination.

191
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:15,357
But somehow, the enemy managed
to find out about our plans.

192
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:19,381
Probably because I was talking
about them all over town, cha-ba-ba!

193
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,340
You again?

194
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:21,877
What's wrong with you?

195
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,437
And what's the point of having a zipper on

196
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:25,317
your mouth if you don't
even use a damn thing?

197
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:28,677
This little buttermouth problem of
yours has got to stop, understand?

198
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:30,877
We're secret agents,
we've got secrets to keep!

199
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:33,077
I want to do it on purpose, Cha-pa-pa!

200
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,417
Why don't you cha-pa-pa me?

201
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,697
I can't believe about it now, cha-pa-pa!

202
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:39,660
There's no need to blame Fukurou!

203
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,417
I don't need a cha-pa-pa!

204
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,088
I take full responsibility!

205
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:44,720
Who wanna go?

206
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,220
Iron body!

207
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,740
I can't even die right!

208
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,437
Oh, just get it over with, you bastard!

209
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,657
You'll be doing everyone a favor!

210
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:57,140
We talked about it, cha-ba-ba! God, ah!

211
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:58,210
You said that...

212
00:13:58,293 --> 00:13:59,123
Enough, I understand.

213
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,360
Hot, hot, hot!

214
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,840
I spilled my coffee again, damn it!

215
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:07,360
Oh, by the way, I heard
Nero didn't work out.

216
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:15,400
We gotta hurry!

217
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,520
Can't you bulls go any faster?

218
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:29,640
So Big Bro Franky sacrificed himself
to save you guys, and now he's...

219
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:31,378
Yeah, that's right.

220
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:35,432
He was trying to rescue Robin
and help us escape with her.

221
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,660
Our Big Bro is such a kind-hearted guy!

222
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:47,780
We need to hurry, or we
won't make it in time.

223
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:52,200
Look, the lights of the Nightless Island!

224
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,660
It's Eni's lobby!

225
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:56,370
Really?

226
00:14:56,453 --> 00:14:57,948
I can't believe we made it!

227
00:14:58,620 --> 00:14:59,450
Alright!

228
00:14:59,533 --> 00:15:00,363
Now we can rescue bro!

229
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,720
Nightless Island?

230
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:07,060
Yeah, the sun never stops
shining there, so it's nightless.

231
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:10,593
They sometimes call the judicial
island a daytime island.

232
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,860
We found him!

233
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:15,940
The giant yoghurt!

234
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:17,810
Luffy!

235
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,110
Luffy!

236
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,960
Hey! Surge!

237
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,440
Who the heck is that?

238
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,297
It's going to be totally fine, okay?

239
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:32,640
It's Strawhats!

240
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:39,840
Looks like we caught up
with him, no problem.

241
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,857
Well, now that we've found the others,

242
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,957
it's time for our date
with the world government.

243
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,580
Hell yeah, it is!

244
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,460
Okay, this is it!

245
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:54,385
Now approaching Innie's lobby!

246
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:57,280
All hands, get ready for a showdown!

247
00:16:08,460 --> 00:16:10,460
Sniper King from Sniper Island?

248
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:13,060
For real? That's right.

249
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:15,017
I'm a close friend of Usopp's.

250
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,477
I'm here because he asked me to
aid you on this perilous journey.

251
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,740
He's a superhero.

252
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:21,337
I knew it.

253
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:24,057
I could totally tell
because of the Masked Cave.

254
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:24,970
Amazing.

255
00:16:25,053 --> 00:16:26,337
I've never seen one before.

256
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:29,480
So wearing a mask and cape
means he has superpowers?

257
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:30,550
Of course!

258
00:16:30,633 --> 00:16:32,837
Everybody in a mask and
cape is a superhero!

259
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:33,750
Oh, really?

260
